{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNormalizationInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNormalizationInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Field","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.ratio_eq_qdim_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.ratio_eq_qdim_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaNormalizationInvariance.lean#L94-L101","doc":"**Both ratios equal the bare q-dimension ratio `d_l²/d_m²`** — the\nnormalization-independent content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.ratio_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.ratio_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaNormalizationInvariance.lean#L82-L92","doc":"**Pruning result: same-block ratios are normalization-invariant.**\nFor any two blocks `l, m` in the same `n` (with `d m ≠ 0`), the ratio of\ngeometric weights equals the ratio of keystone weights — the `F/D²` factor\ncancels. Consequence: the C1 normalization choice cannot change any generation\nobservable expressed as a same-`n` ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.wKey_sum_eq_Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.wKey_sum_eq_Z","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaNormalizationInvariance.lean#L75-L80","doc":"**Keystone weight sums to the defect `Z = D²/F`, not `1`.** This is the\n`Z(n)` of the defect script: `Σ_{λ∈s} d_q²/F = (Σ d_q²)/F = D²/F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.wPlanch_sum_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.wPlanch_sum_one","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaNormalizationInvariance.lean#L67-L73","doc":"**Geometric weight is a probability measure.** `Σ_{λ∈s} d_q²/D² = 1`\n(`D² = Σ d_q²` by construction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.wPlanch_eq_global_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.wPlanch_eq_global_factor","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaNormalizationInvariance.lean#L58-L65","doc":"**The normalization change is one λ-independent global factor.**\n`wPlanch = (F/D²) · wKey`. The geometric and keystone weights are proportional\nwith a constant (`F/D²`) that does not depend on the block `λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.wKey","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.wKey","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaNormalizationInvariance.lean#L55-L56","doc":"Keystone weight `W_λ = d_q(λ)²/F` with `F = [n]_q!` (the consumer form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.wPlanch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.wPlanch","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaNormalizationInvariance.lean#L51-L53","doc":"Geometric / RT–Verlinde Plancherel weight `w_λ = d_q(λ)²/D²` (Beasley–Witten\nlocalization output; the true probability measure). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.D2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaNorm.D2","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaNormalizationInvariance.lean#L48-L49","doc":"Global quantum dimension `D² = Σ_{λ∈s} d_q(λ)²` of an `n`-block. ","signatureChunk":0}]}